WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.300
Good morning, John! It's Question Tuesday on Friday.

00:00:03.300 --> 00:00:06.600
The day that we answer real questions from real Nerdfighters. Go!

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.480
Question Hank: What country is Nerdfighteria bigger than?

00:00:10.480 --> 00:00:12.480
Hank: Uhhh... who're you?

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.100
Question Hank: I'm the you that asks the questions.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:16.900
Hank: Thaaat's not normal.

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:19.400
Question Hank: Yeah, I don't think that we do normal.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:24.500
Like, the last video you did, you used the phrase "passive-aggressive robot sack of ketchup pee,"

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.400
and the one before that was about cat gifs [GU-ifs].

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.400
Hank: Did you just say "gifs" [GU-ifs]?

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.600
Because we say "gifs" [jifs].
Not that either of those are incorrect.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.400
Question Hank: Yeah, actually, I'm thinking about changing,

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:36.400
because the president used "gif" [GU-if] in one of his speeches.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.200
Hank: Well, I'm not thinking about changing, and you're me!

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:44.400
Question Hank: Yeah, that's not, uh... whatever. 
What countries is Nerdfighteria bigger than?

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:46.500
Hank: Well, that depends on how you count.

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:51.600
Uh, I've done some research on this topic, and if you're counting by the number of people who watch regularly,

00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:54.600
we are bigger than 61 countries, including the Barbados,

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:58.100
and if you count by the number of people subscribed, we're bigger than 85 countries,

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:02.300
including Djibouti, which has the smallest population of all countries in Africa.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.700
Trivia Hank: It also contains the lowest point in all of Africa.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.900
The shores of Lake Assal are more than 500 feet below sea level.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:13.500
Hank: Ehhhhh... that is... just got used to the question-asking me! Who the heck are you?!

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:15.300
Trivia Hank: I'm Useless Trivia You.

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:19.400
Did you know that volleyball was invented as a safer alternative to basketball in the 1890s?

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.500
Hank: No, of course I didn't know that! No one knew that!

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.700
Question Hank: Thoughts on YouTube paid subscriptions?

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:27.700
Yeah, I don't know, uh, how people are going to end up using them.

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:30.100
Hopefully, in innovative and interesting ways.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:33.800
I am in favor of people being able to make money from the content they produce,

00:01:33.800 --> 00:01:37.700
but I will tell you that John and I will never put our content behind a paywall.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.800
Trivia Hank: Did you know that the first picture uploaded to the internet

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:43.100
was of an all-female comedy group based at the CERN Laboratory in Switzerland?

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.500
Question Hank: Is Batman really a superhero, or just a super rich guy?

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:52.600
Hank: I mean, there are a lot of super rich guys that didn't become Batman.

00:01:52.600 --> 00:01:56.100
I would almost venture to say that Batman is more of a superhero than other superheroes,

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:59.000
because he doesn't have anything that makes him super special.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:02.900
He doesn't have any mystical super powers. 
He just has a bunch of money.

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.900
Trivia Hank: Cousin Larry from Perfect Strangers would have played a villain called Man Bat

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:09.400
in a cancelled follow-up to the George Clooney Batman movie.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:13.400
Hank: Wow, you are both amazing and terrible.

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:15.400
Question Hank: Can you teach me how to Dougie?

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:18.000
Hank: No...
Trivia Hank: I can, (No!) I can teach you how to do the Dougie!

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:21.300
Question Hank: How can light be affected by black holes if it has no mass?

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.400
Henry Reich: Well, Hank, gravity is actually an interaction between

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:27.700
the objects with energy and momentum, which light has.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.800
Trivia Hank:  Was I just momentarily replaced by the guy from Minute Physics?

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:36.700
Also, did you know that he's actually a really good mandolin player?

00:02:37.100 --> 00:02:40.900
(Henry plays the guitar)

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.900
Question Hank: Marvel or DC?

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.000
Hank: Dark Horse.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.400
Trivia Hank: Stan Lee's birth name is Stanley.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:55.200
Hank: Just to be clear, all the extra Hanks in this video did not streamline the process.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.800
So yeah! Two Question Tuesdays in one week... what?

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:00.700
I will say, though, mine was little bit more ambitious.

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:03.600
But! The best answers of this week's Question Tuesday?

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.000
Those definitely go to Nerdfighteria.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.500
Like Patrick McGuire, who said that if he were invisible,

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:09.300
he would to to Paris and beat up a mime.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:14.700
But not to be mean, no, because the applause that he would get, the recognition would be astounding.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:16.800
And then there's Rachel's take on the Great Gatsby film.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:20.500
Quoting Gatsby, saying, "Whenever you feel like criticizing anyone,

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:23.800
just remember that all the people in this world haven't had the advantages that you've had."

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:26.300
Her take on the movie, thus, being that the people who created it

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:30.100
must not have had the same advantages she had in having read the book.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:33.600
And then there's the Vampiress, here, who is excited about ferrets.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:35.200
They totally are tiny dog otters!

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.100
So, thanks, Nerdfighteria, you guys are good at answering questions.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:41.200
You should feel free to answer the questions that I just answered, even though there weren't that many of them,

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:42.200
because of all of the whip panning.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:43.800
Thanks to all of the people who helped with that:

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:46.900
Henry from Minute Physics, Stefan, and Emily and Michael

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:48.800
were all in this room while we were doing that.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:51.000
John, don't do a Question Tuesday next Tuesday,

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.300
because that would definitely be overkill. I'll see you then.

00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:57.900
[Cali Swag: Teach Me How to Dougie]

